    Largest Rectangle — The Clever Part
    We already know:  When a smaller bar arrives, it tells us the right boundary of taller bars.
    The question is:  How do we know the left boundary?

Consider:   heights = [2, 5, 6, 2]
            index     0  1  2  3

Before processing the final 2, our stack contains:   [0, 1, 2]
with heights:                                        [2, 5, 6]

