            "For each bar, I want to determine the maximum width over which that bar can 
                remain the limiting height. That width is bounded by the first smaller bar on the left and 
                the first smaller bar on the right. I maintain an increasing monotonic stack of indices. 
                When I encounter a smaller bar, the current index becomes the right boundary for 
                all taller bars popped from the stack. After popping, the new stack top gives 
                the previous smaller boundary. Therefore, for a popped bar, the width is 
                    currentIndex - stack.peek() - 1, with -1 as the left boundary when the stack 
                becomes empty. Each index is pushed and popped at most once, 
                giving O(n) amortized time and O(n) auxiliary space."

