The stack is increasing because it gives us the boundary information we need efficiently.

L5-level explanation

        "I maintain an increasing monotonic stack of bar indices so that for every bar in 
            the stack, I know that there has not yet been a smaller bar to its right. 
            When a smaller bar arrives, it becomes the first smaller element to the right 
            for the taller bars being popped. After popping, the new stack top gives the previous 
            smaller element on the left. Therefore, popping a bar tells me that both boundaries 
            needed to calculate its maximum possible rectangle are now known."

That's the key.

