🔥 Important distinction
    
    Compare the three problems we've learned:
    
    Next Greater Element
                        Stack = decreasing
                        
                        Waiting for → GREATER
                        Pop when → current > stack.top
    Daily Temperatures
                        Stack = decreasing
                        
                        Waiting for → WARMER
                        Pop when → current > stack.top
    Largest Rectangle
                        Stack = increasing
                        
                        Waiting for → SMALLER
                        Pop when → current < stack.top
    
    The common pattern is:
    
            Elements enter the stack because their answer is not known yet. 
            A future element arrives and resolves them, so we pop them.
    
    That is the real Monotonic Stack pattern.
